clearcote: WebGPU adapter architecture follows the GPU model; a capture's own value is read.

Two defects in one seam. The profile importer read the WebGPU identity from webgpu.vendor /
webgpu.architecture, but captures store it under webgpu.info.*, so a donor's correct value was
never read and the fallback always fired. The fallback pinned the architecture per vendor: every
NVIDIA persona said "ampere" (a GTX 1060 is Pascal), every AMD one "rdna2" (a spelling real
Chrome never emits; Dawn says "rdna-2"). Now the importer reads webgpu.info.* first, the fallback
derives the architecture from the model the renderer string names using the modal value of real
decontaminated Windows captures, and the validator rejects a derived architecture that disagrees
with the model or a desktop spelling outside the vocabulary real Chrome uses (a captured identity
only warns: dual-GPU laptops legitimately disagree). REPRO gains wgpuarch=.

